    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0564" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg490"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 159.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-01-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 29, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose for your information A copy of
                    Mr. Adams’s despatch,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d383-f1"/> No. 1126, of the 4th of
                    January, and its accompaniments, relative to the disposition of the Osborne
                    flotilla, it being a reply to my instructions to him upon that subject, in
                    compliance with your suggestion.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d383-f1" n="*" xml:id="d383-f1-content">
                <p>For enclosure see correspondence with Great Britain.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
